{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788112102,"nonce":"akCbQuOxn+GroarPLZwBDZSu7w8=","title":"2.5 PNG render channel (baseviz)","message":"Wave 2 — eyes. Depends: 2.4 (things dump), baseviz. CLI-side (python), no C#\nbeyond the dump verb.\n\n## Goal\nThe PNG channel: render any map rect as an image the agent Reads directly —\nthe independent second check on textual spatial reasoning, and Dorian's\nat-a-glance view of what the agent built.\n\n## Context (read first)\n- `rimworld-tools/baseviz/` (canvas.py, catalog.py, ir.py, server.py) — reuse\n  its catalog + rendering; extend in rimworld-tools, keep autorimmer thin\n- 2.4 things/terrain dump; 2.3 landmark registry\n\n## Scope\n- In-mod: `map dump --rect …` → terrain + things + zones grid (superset of\n  baseviz IR; worker defines the delta, coordinates with ir.py round-trip).\n- CLI: `rwa render --rect … --out file.png [--layers …] [--landmarks]\n  [--scale N]` → PNG via baseviz-style canvas; legend strip optional; ruler\n  marks optional.\n- Colors/glyphs from the runtime catalog (mod-aware, bench-version stable).\n\n## Invariants\nNo game-side image rendering; render is pure function of dump + catalog\n(same dump → same PNG).\n\n## Open questions (worker's)\nDump format vs IR exactly; zoom/scale defaults; how pawns/items-on-ground\nrender; whether to also emit the dump as importable baseviz IR (nice-to-have).\n\n## Acceptance\nRender of a built base is legible: an agent shown ONLY the PNG correctly\nanswers room count, door locations, and which room holds the stove. Same dump\ntwice → byte-identical PNG.","files":null}]}